From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Norman Herms <dockseed@proton.me>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 20:51:18 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: allwinner: a733: Add the S_TWI2 controller

The SoC dtsi describes S_TWI0 and S_TWI1 of the CPUS domain, but not
S_TWI2. A board that brings its pins out on a pin header cannot use it.

Add S_TWI2 at 0x07085000 (A733 manual, memory map), interrupt SPI 205
(12.2.3.1), with its bus gate and reset in the PRCM (4.2.5.16). The
manual gives it the registers of TWI0 (18.11.7), so the node has the
compatible of S_TWI0 and S_TWI1.

Add the pin group the Radxa Cubie A7S can use: SDA on PL5 and SCK on
PM4, both function 3 (18.14.3.1, tables 18-38 and 18-39). The board
routes PL5 to pin 22 of J11 and PM4 to pin 3 of J6, so the bus spans
both pin headers; no other S_TWI2 pin reaches a header. The pins carry
other functions as well, so a board uses one function on them. The node
is disabled; a board enables it.

Not covered: DMA requests, which the driver does not use.

Tested on Radxa Cubie A7S: the controller drives SDA on PL5 and SCK on
PM4, read back on two GPIOs wired to the header pins.

Assisted-by: LLM
---
 .../arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun60i-a733.dtsi | 20 +++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 20 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun60i-a733.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun60i-a733.dtsi
index d384bb753c36..cf78be254f5a 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun60i-a733.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun60i-a733.dtsi
@@ -1786,6 +1786,13 @@ r_i2c1_pl12_pins: r-i2c1-pl12-pins {
 				function = "r_i2c1";
 			};
 
+			/omit-if-no-ref/
+			r_i2c2_pl5_pm4_pins: r-i2c2-pl5-pm4-pins {
+				pins = "PL5", "PM4";
+				allwinner,pinmux = <3>;
+				function = "r_i2c2";
+			};
+
 			/omit-if-no-ref/
 			r_ir_rx_pl6_pin: r-ir-rx-pl6-pin {
 				pins = "PL6";
@@ -1930,6 +1937,19 @@ r_i2c1: i2c@7084000 {
 			#size-cells = <0>;
 		};
 
+		r_i2c2: i2c@7085000 {
+			compatible = "allwinner,sun60i-a733-i2c",
+				     "allwinner,sun8i-v536-i2c",
+				     "allwinner,sun6i-a31-i2c";
+			reg = <0x07085000 0x400>;
+			interrupts = <GIC_SPI 205 IRQ_TYPE_LEVEL_HIGH 0>;
+			clocks = <&r_ccu CLK_BUS_R_I2C2>;
+			resets = <&r_ccu RST_BUS_R_I2C2>;
+			status = "disabled";
+			#address-cells = <1>;
+			#size-cells = <0>;
+		};
+
 		rtc: rtc@7090000 {
 			compatible = "allwinner,sun60i-a733-rtc",
 				     "allwinner,sun50i-r329-rtc";
